# CAMEL OVERKILL: HUMP-P "POWER MANAGER". Four new batteries feed ONLY the engine and the two ballast pumps; the two
# vanilla batteries keep feeding the nav terminal, status monitor and gun capacitors (critical bus).
# ALL battery charging comes out of the reactor's surplus, so a battery suddenly charging can never brown out the main bus.
name camel_propulsion
box battery
note "HUMP-P POWER MANAGER: HOW IT WORKS" "Main bus demand = reactor load - battery charging, averaged over two ticks. All charging flows through the CHARGE TAP relay, whose load_value_out is exactly what the batteries draw.\nWanted charge: propulsion = its bus load + (80 - charge %) x 40 kW (0..2000), so it hovers at 80 %; critical = (100 - charge %) x 40 kW (0..1000), kept full.\nReactor setpoint (out2 -> HUMP-1) = main demand + both wants + 1000 kW while the governor is about to switch the oxygen generator on (7212).\nSurplus = reactor output - main demand. Critical bank takes min(surplus, its want), propulsion takes the rest. The game rounds each battery's rate to 10 % (50 kW): every battery gets an equal share in 50 kW steps and one battery (rotating every 30 s) takes the remainder, so the banks stay level and the total is exact. So when the reactor lags behind a step the charging gives way instead of the voltage, and a sudden drop in load is soaked up.\nPropulsion below 25 % -> 1 on 7209 (alert YELLOW). Telemetry: 7202 propulsion charge %, 7211 propulsion kW."
note "WIRING" "in1 charge_%, in2 load_value_out from ONE propulsion battery\nin4 <- CHARGE TAP relay load_value_out\nin5 charge_% from ONE critical (vanilla) battery\nin3 reactor load_value_out, in6 reactor power_value_out\nout1, out5, out6, out7 -> set_rate of propulsion batteries 1..4, out3 -> their disable_output (held 0)\nout4, out8 -> set_rate of critical batteries 1, 2\nout2 -> HUMP-1 in8 (setpoint kW)"
c txc wifi Channel=7202
c txl wifi Channel=7211
c txw wifi Channel=7209
c k25 mem Value=25
c low greater
w k25.out low.1
w low.out txw.in
# --- main bus demand = reactor load - battery charging (measured by the CHARGE TAP relay that feeds both banks)
c base00 sub
w in3 base00.1
w in4 base00.2
# the oxygen generator (1000 kW) switches in one tick: take it out of the filter and add it back from the relay
# command itself (7213), so a switch-off is soaked up by the batteries at once instead of 0.3 s later
c rxg wifi Channel=7213
c k1000 mem Value=1000
c gkw mul
w rxg.out gkw.1
w k1000.out gkw.2
c base0 sub
w base00.out base0.1
w gkw.out base0.2
# low-pass for the reactor setpoint (x 0.9 old + 0.1 new per tick): the two loads can arrive a tick apart
c base mem Value=0
c f9 mem Value=0.9
c f1 mem Value=0.1
c bo mul
c bn mul
c bs add
w base.out bo.1
w f9.out bo.2
w base0.out bn.1
w f1.out bn.2
w bo.out bs.1
w bn.out bs.2
w bs.out base.in
c basef add
w base.out basef.1
w gkw.out basef.2
# --- wants
c k80 mem Value=80
c k100 mem Value=100
c kg mem Value=40
c errp sub
c biasp mul
c wantp add ClampMin=0 ClampMax=2000
w k80.out errp.1
w in1 errp.2 low.2 txc.in
w errp.out biasp.1
w kg.out biasp.2
w in2 wantp.1 txl.in
w biasp.out wantp.2
c errc sub
c biasc mul ClampMin=0 ClampMax=1000
w k100.out errc.1
w in5 errc.2
w errc.out biasc.1
w kg.out biasc.2
# --- setpoint
c rxo wifi Channel=7212
c pre mul
w rxo.out pre.1
w k1000.out pre.2
c sp1 add
c sp2 add
c sp3 add
w basef.out sp1.1
w wantp.out sp1.2
w sp1.out sp2.1
w biasc.out sp2.2
w sp2.out sp3.1
w pre.out sp3.2
w sp3.out out2
# --- share the surplus: critical first (min(surplus, want)), propulsion gets the rest
c sur sub
w in6 sur.1
w basef.out sur.2
c md sub
c ma abs
c ms add
c mm sub
c k2 mem Value=2
c cmin div ClampMin=0
w sur.out md.1 ms.1
w biasc.out md.2 ms.2
w md.out ma.in
w ms.out mm.1
w ma.out mm.2
w mm.out cmin.1
w k2.out cmin.2
# equal split in 50 kW steps: the game rounds each battery's rate to 10 % (50 kW here). Every battery gets
# q = floor(T / (N x 50)) x 10 %, and ONE battery also takes the remainder r. Which one rotates every 30 s, so over
# time all of them charge the same and the banks stay level, while the total is always exact.
#   propulsion (N=4, T 0..2000): f = floor(T/200), q = 10 f %, r = T/5 - 40 f %
#   critical   (N=2, T 0..1000): f = floor(T/100), q = 10 f %, r = T/5 - 20 f %
c zero mem Value=0
c osc osc OutputType=Pulse Frequency=0.0333
c rot mem Value=0
c k1 mem Value=1
c inc add
c m4 mod Modulus=4
c m2 mod Modulus=2
w rot.out inc.1 m2.in
w osc.out inc.2
w inc.out m4.in
w m4.out rot.in
c k5 mem Value=5
c k10 mem Value=10
c k20c mem Value=20
c k40 mem Value=40
c k200 mem Value=200
c k3 mem Value=3
# critical bank
c cT div ClampMin=0 ClampMax=10
c cf floor
c cq mul
c c5 div
c c20 mul
c cr sub ClampMin=0
w cmin.out cT.1 c5.1
w k100.out cT.2
w cT.out cf.in
w cf.out cq.1 c20.1
w k10.out cq.2
w k20c.out c20.2
w k5.out c5.2
w c5.out cr.1
w c20.out cr.2
c ce0 equals
c ce1 equals
c cx0 mul
c cx1 mul
c ca0 add ClampMax=100
c ca1 add ClampMax=100
w m2.out ce0.1 ce1.1
w zero.out ce0.2
w k1.out ce1.2
w ce0.out cx0.1
w ce1.out cx1.1
w cr.out cx0.2 cx1.2
w cq.out ca0.1 ca1.1
w cx0.out ca0.2
w cx1.out ca1.2
w ca0.out out4
w ca1.out out8
# propulsion bank
c rest sub
w sur.out rest.1
w cmin.out rest.2
c restc add ClampMin=0 ClampMax=2000
w rest.out restc.1
w zero.out restc.2
c pT div
c pf floor
c pq mul
c p5 div
c p40 mul
c pr sub ClampMin=0
w restc.out pT.1 p5.1
w k200.out pT.2
w pT.out pf.in
w pf.out pq.1 p40.1
w k10.out pq.2
w k40.out p40.2
w k5.out p5.2
w p5.out pr.1
w p40.out pr.2
c pe0 equals
c pe1 equals
c pe2 equals
c pe3 equals
c px0 mul
c px1 mul
c px2 mul
c px3 mul
c pa0 add ClampMax=100
c pa1 add ClampMax=100
c pa2 add ClampMax=100
c pa3 add ClampMax=100
c k2r mem Value=2
w rot.out pe0.1 pe1.1 pe2.1 pe3.1
w zero.out pe0.2
w k1.out pe1.2
w k2r.out pe2.2
w k3.out pe3.2
w pe0.out px0.1
w pe1.out px1.1
w pe2.out px2.1
w pe3.out px3.1
w pr.out px0.2 px1.2 px2.2 px3.2
w pq.out pa0.1 pa1.1 pa2.1 pa3.1
w px0.out pa0.2
w px1.out pa1.2
w px2.out pa2.2
w px3.out pa3.2
w pa0.out out1
w pa1.out out5
w pa2.out out6
w pa3.out out7
c k0 mem Value=0
w k0.out out3
